Keep the drafter quantized when the checkpoint says it is

`_mtp_quant_config` disables quantization for every `modelopt_mixed` checkpoint on the
grounds that "Serialized Qwen3.5 ModelOpt checkpoints keep embedded MTP weights in BF16".
That holds for the Qwen3.5 exports it was written against. It does not hold for
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, whose own quantization_config names the drafter's experts:

    mtp.layers.0.mlp.experts.up_proj -> {"quant_algo": "NVFP4", "group_size": 16}

So the MTP module is built unquantized at full hidden size while the loader hands it the
NVFP4 tensor-parallel shard, and a TP=2 start dies before it serves:

    eagle_worker_v2.py:203  -> qwen3_5_mtp.py load_weights
      -> fused_moe_triton/layer.py _load_w13  expert_data.copy_(loaded_weight)
    RuntimeError: The size of tensor a (2560) must match the size of tensor b (1280)
                  at non-singleton dimension 1

Reproduced on generations 149, 160 and 163 of a two-box GB10 pair, and the same code is
unchanged at upstream f70e8c68 (2026-10-05), so no image bump avoids it.

The fix asks the checkpoint instead of assuming: if its own `quantized_layers` cover any
`mtp.*` entry, the drafter is quantized and must be built that way. This mirrors the Quark
branch immediately below, which already detects per checkpoint rather than per scheme —
there by reading the exclude list, here by reading the include list. A checkpoint that
really does ship a BF16 drafter names no `mtp.*` layer and still takes the old path.

--- a/python/sglang/srt/models/qwen3_5_mtp.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/models/qwen3_5_mtp.py
@@ -55,6 +55,21 @@
     quantized; the loader's fusion gate has to see the same normalization the
     constructor applies, or it would answer for the target's quantization.
     """
+    # ASK THE CHECKPOINT BEFORE ASSUMING THE DRAFTER IS BF16. The branch below is right for
+    # the Qwen3.5 exports it was written for and wrong for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, which names
+    # its drafter's experts in its own quantization_config:
+    #   mtp.layers.0.mlp.experts.up_proj -> {"quant_algo": "NVFP4", "group_size": 16}
+    # Building that unquantized allocates full hidden size while the loader supplies the TP
+    # shard, and the start dies in _load_w13 on 2560 against 1280 at TP=2 before it serves.
+    # Same shape of check as the Quark branch below: per checkpoint, not per scheme.
+    if quant_config is not None:
+        quantized_layers = getattr(quant_config, "quantized_layers", None) or {}
+        if any(
+            isinstance(name, str) and (name.startswith("mtp.") or ".mtp." in name)
+            for name in quantized_layers
+        ):
+            return quant_config
+
     # Serialized Qwen3.5 ModelOpt checkpoints keep embedded MTP weights in
     # BF16. Disable quantization for those checkpoints; non-serialized
     # modelopt_fp4 still converts MoE expert weights on load.
